  "claim": "Clark County in a western state contains both the City of Las Vegas and another college. Craig Heyer played baseball at that college. Cymopterus cinerarius is native to the state.",
  "evidencia": "Page: College of Southern Nevada. Sentence: The College of Southern Nevada (CSN) is primarily a two-year college in Clark County, Nevada, with four four-year degrees in Dental Hygiene, Medical Lab Scientist, Respiratory Sciences, and Fire & Emergency Services Admin.\nPage: Clark County, Nevada. Sentence: Las Vegas, Nevada's most populous city, has been the county seat since the county was established.\nPage: Craig Heyer. Sentence: Prior to becoming a professional, Heyer played college baseball at the College of Southern Nevada and University of Nevada, Las Vegas (UNLV).\nPage: Cymopterus cinerarius. Sentence: This small plant is native to the US states of California and Nevada, where it grows on the rocky talus of the Sierra Nevada.",
